# Coverage configuration for Go projects
# This file documents coverage settings and exclusion patterns

# Default coverage threshold (can be overridden with COVERAGE_THRESHOLD env var)
# Industry standard: 70-80% for most projects, 80%+ for critical systems
COVERAGE_THRESHOLD=75

# Files and patterns to exclude from coverage calculation
# Add patterns here for files that should not count towards coverage:
# - Generated files
# - Test utilities
# - Mock files
# - Vendor code

# Example exclusion patterns (uncomment as needed):
# **/mocks/**
# **/*_mock.go
# **/testdata/**
# **/vendor/**
# **/*.pb.go
# **/generated/**

# Coverage modes:
# - set: did each statement run?
# - count: how many times did each statement run?
# - atomic: like count, but counts precisely in parallel programs

# We use atomic mode for accurate parallel test coverage
COVERAGE_MODE=atomic

# Notes:
# - Coverage reports are generated in backend/coverage.html
# - Raw coverage data is in backend/coverage.out
# - Use COVERAGE_THRESHOLD env var to adjust threshold per environment
# - Pre-commit hooks will fail if coverage drops below threshold
